            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="0606" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-18T10:00:00+08:00">May 18, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 18—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>209. 1. We learn from informed officials that the Ministry of Railways signed May
                    12 a preliminary agreement with French banking <pb facs="0607" n="599"
                        xml:id="pg599"/> interests for a loan of pounds sterling 4 million for
                    construction of a railway from Kunming (Yunnanful) to Kweiyang. The banks at
                    present included are the Banque Franco-Chinoise and the Banque de L’Indo-Chine;
                    it is stated that other French banks will join in the final agreement.</p>
                <p>2. Sent to the Department, to Peiping, Shanghai, Yunnanfu, Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
